      loading="lazy"
    />
    <figcaption>Concentric rings around a glowing core. Effects like "Pulse Rings" and "Centrifugal Rings" send each wave outward from the centre; the jagged edges follow the spectrum.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>
    In "Pulse Rings", rings expand from a beating core, modulated by the spectrum. "Centrifugal Rings" goes one step further: every frame of the spectrum is born as its own ring and travels outward, so a beat becomes a thick wave. "Audio Sphere" is a raymarched sphere whose surface is displaced by the spectrum, and "Blobs" lets soft spheres merge and pop apart again while the bass inflates them.
  </p>

  <h3>Light, Stage and Laser</h3>

  <figure class="blog-demo">
    <img
      src="/image/visualizer-blog-2.png"
      alt="Audio visualizer Light Rays effect: bright volumetric rays in white, blue and violet shooting out from a glowing centre in all directions"
      width="1920"
      height="1080"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <figcaption>"Light Rays": volumetric rays from a bright core. Each ray is assigned to a frequency range and grows longer as that range gets louder.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>
    Beyond "Light Rays" there is a whole stage rig: "Stage Lights" shine down through fog from a truss, "Footlights" beam upward from the stage edge, and "Corner Beams", "Side Lights" and "Searchlights" swing their cones to the beat. The "Colour Organ" quotes the 70s with three frosted panels for bass, mids and treble. Eleven laser effects, from "Laser Fan" through "Laser Spirograph" to "Laser Oscilloscope", draw thin beams in fog where bass and mids set the geometry and onsets re-orient the figure. Four disco effects add a mirror ball, sweeping reflections and a lit dance floor.
  </p>

  <h3>Tunnels and Space</h3>

  <figure class="blog-demo">
    <img
      src="/image/visualizer-blog-3.png"
      alt="Audio visualizer tunnel effect: concentric glowing rings and radial blue light beams leading into a dark centre"
      width="1920"
